  "verbalization": "Ancistrobenomine A is implicated in the regulation of SN12K1 through a multi-step mechanism involving Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. This enzyme is a target of both Ancistrobenomine A and another compound, (6aR,9R)-N-[(1S,2S,4R,7S)-2-hydroxy-5-oxo-4,7-di(propan-2-yl)-3-oxa-6,9-diazatricyclo[7.3.0.02,6]dodecan-4-yl]-7-methyl-6,6a,8,9-tetrahydro-4H-indolo[4,3-fg]quinoline-9-carboxamide, which itself targets SN12K1. The presence of multiple targets at the Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like level suggests a potential role in modulating SN12K1 activity through enzymatic regulation. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ancistrobenomine A and SN12K1, with the potential for a broader regulatory pathway involving other compounds that interact with the same target. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like in mediating the effects of Ancistrobenomine A on SN12K1, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
